  "notes": "Modified cash basis village (recorded as basis cash). Governmental lines from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); the statement rolls fund balances 250,391 -> 287,128 (p5): + revenues 347,813 - expenditures 404,431 + transfers from other funds 93,355 (Total column after eliminations; General Fund's 19,000 to other funds eliminated). Intergovernmental 82,018 split by the all-fund budget schedule's breakdown (p8: highway allocation 53,894, municipal equalization 18,010, motor vehicle fees 4,003, other intergovernmental 6,111; ties exactly), as in FY2023; the Street and Alley Fund's 76,059 does not tie to those lines and stays whole in detail. Governmental ending cash 270,439 and certificates of deposit 6,987 as printed (p3); county treasurer cash 1,248 and restricted cash 8,454 separate lines, not added. Business-type lines from the modified cash proprietary statement (p7), which ties to the government-wide modified cash Statement of Activities (p2: charges 435,281, expenditures 304,559, transfers (93,355), net position 43,508 -> 80,875); measure cash (net position consists only of cash). The accrual-basis proprietary statements (pp9-11, supplementary) are not used; proprietary is null for a cash-basis report (as FY2023). Balance sheet: governmental lines from p3 (totals equal the government-wide governmental column 287,128), business-type from p1. Detail: the only supplementary schedule in the trim is the combined all-fund-types Budgetary Comparison Schedule (p8), so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds (p4) and proprietary funds (p7) statements; budget_final null. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
